s`, `other_columns`, `is_compound`, `on_delete` and `on_update`. `column` and `other_column` are excluded from comparison. It is no longer a tuple, so unpacking it raises `TypeError`.\n- **Reading keys:** `Table.foreign_keys` groups `PRAGMA foreign_key_list` rows by `id` and reads the actions back.\n- **Creating keys:** `resolve_foreign_keys`, `create_table_sql` and `add_foreign_keys` accept compound keys and emit a table-level `FOREIGN KEY (...) REFERENCES ...` line. They also write `ON UPDATE`/`ON DELETE`. `add_foreign_keys` accepts `ForeignKey` objects directly.\n- **Keeping keys:** `transform_sql` drops keys by column name or exact column tuple, renames their columns, and keeps their actions.\n- **Other methods:** `add_foreign_key` takes `on_delete`/`on_update` and compound columns. `index_foreign_keys` creates one composite index per compound key.\n\nChoices I made where the spec was silent:\n- `add_foreign_keys` raises the existing \"Compound foreign key must have the same number of columns on both sides\" error when a 4-tuple's two sides differ in length. The spec only covered that check for `add_foreign_key`.\n- Dedup in `add_foreign_keys` matches on columns, other table and other columns only. A key that differs only in its actions is skipped, as the spec says.\n\nI did not edit any tests or docs. Black isn't installed in the venv, so I did not run a formatter. I wrapped the one overlong signature by hand, and a few new lines are longer than black's 88 columns.", "ttft_ms": 1216, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 153550, "uuid": "931d0f42-0867-4010-ad76-332744a66883", "ttft_stream_ms": 878, "time_to_request_ms": 197, "first_content_frame_ms": 878, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
